          "id": "SP_MODEERIA_ROTUNDA",
          "name": "Modeeria rotunda",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Snow Globe Jelly",
          "lineage": "Modeeria",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Stolonal colonies, a filiform hydrorhiza giving rise to small hydrothecae on short pedicels (Fig. 4 A). Hydrotheca tubiform, with basal circular diaphragm (Fig. 4 B). Hydrothecal rim uneven, with two large cusps, separated by two large embayments (Fig. 4 A). Operculum composed of two semi-circular, pleated valves, attached to rim embayments and closing as a roof. Measurements (in µm). Hydrotheca: diameter at aperture 220 – 230; height, up to diaphragm 730 – 800, diameter at diaphragm 80 – 100, length of pedicel 100.",
